          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Boris Pasternak's Early Life</strong><br>\nBoris Pasternak was born on February 10, 1890, in Moscow, Russia, into a prominent Jewish family. His father was a talented painter and his mother a renowned concert pianist, which meant that art and culture surrounded Boris from a young age. He began writing seriously during his university years, although he started studying to become a composer. Boris was influenced by the 1917 Russian Revolution, which became a significant theme in his later works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Literary Career Beginnings</strong><br>\nPasternak's early work was marked by his passion for philosophy and his unique lyrical style. His first book of poems, \"My Sister, Life,\" is considered one of the most influential collections in Russian literature. The book's publication in 1922 won him a broad readership. His poetry often dealt with themes of love, nature, and art, reflecting his belief in the transformative power of literature.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Shift to Prose</strong><br>\nDuring the 1930s, Pasternak increasingly turned to prose, translating many significant works into Russian, including those of Shakespeare, Goethe, and Schiller. This was partly due to the changing political climate in the Soviet Union, which made the personal and introspective nature of his poetry risky. His translations are still celebrated for their linguistic beauty and precision.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
